    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Consume Flesh",
      "actions": 1,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "manipulate"
      ],
      "text": "Requirements The ghoul is adjacent to the corpse of a creature that died within the last hour.\n\n---\n\nEffect The ghoul devours a chunk of the corpse and regains 7d6 healing Hit Points. It can regain Hit Points from any given corpse only once.\n\nShe also absorbs a portion of the memories once possessed by the creature she fed upon, potentially revealing secrets held by the flesh at the GM's discretion, and also gains a +1 status bonus to all skill checks for 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Ghoul Fever",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "disease"
      ],
      "text": "Saving Throw DC 32 Fortitude save\n\n---\n\nStage 1 carrier with no ill effect (1 day)\n\nStage 2 2d6 void damage and regains half as many Hit Points from all healing (1 day)\n\nStage 3 as stage 2 (1 day)\n\nStage 4 2d6 void damage and gains no benefit from healing (1 day)\n\nStage 5 as stage 4 (1 day)\n\nStage 6 dead, and rises as a Ghoul the next midnight."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Paralysis",
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "incapacitation",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "Any living, non-elf creature hit by a ghoul's attack must succeed at a DC 32 Fortitude save save or become Paralyzed. It can attempt a new save at the end of each of its turns, and the DC cumulatively decreases by 1 on each such save."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Recall Memory",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "concentrate"
      ],
      "text": "Frequency once per day\n\n---\n\nEffect Yurgak focuses her thoughts and recalls a memory from a previously fed-upon corpse. She can attempt to Recall Knowledge using any Lore as if she has legendary proficiency with it (+26 on the check).",
